## What I Did As An Intern

From talking to many auditors,I discovered that auditors spent dozens of hours per quarter on repeatable data pulls and consent checks. After working with auditors to understand their pain points, I built Alteryx and Python pipelines to automate a recurring task from 40+ hours per quarter to 90 seconds for 90% of cases. 
I also partnered with an SVP on SQL-driven consumer consent compliance for CD and IRA workstreams.

## What I Did As A Full-Time Analyst
As a full-time analyst, I was selected by peer vote to present AI simulations to 1,000+ live and global virtual attendees. I presented on how AI simulations (or generative agent-based modeling) can be used to explore risk scenarios and inform decision-making, saving the Bank time, money, and resources.

## What I Learned

If you find a problem, design a solution. Design is everywhere.
